19:## Never
25:6. Leave a rule of engagement unstated or a graded question settled by silence. Rules of engagement (scope, which files may change, tools, procedural order, every negative) are always stated in a file the agent can read (IN-15 01:45; AL-1 carve-out 05:21). A deliverable-property rule (format, literal, ordering, rounding, precedence, tie-break, null condition, merge winner) is either stated, or settled by one determinate shipped fact that contradicts every wrong reading and is listed in `WORK/EVIDENCE_MAP.md` (AL-1 05:21-32, FC:492; LEVER_RULES 0b). Silence never settles anything (05:27): unmapped lookup codes, malformed reference rows, a branch that never fires on shipped data, readings that coincide on shipped data, and pronouns with two antecedents still need a sentence. "QC deferred" is never a pass for IN-16.
27:8. Explain a trap in any agent-visible file (W1, hard rule; QC IN-17 01:47 fails the same act). No "not only X", no "note that", no "be careful", no trap lists, no rule counts in the instruction, no sentence that names the wrong reading, and no sentence announcing a property, edge case or branch the shipped input already establishes. State the rule; never state how it is usually misread. No self-check paragraph in the instruction. Allowed and required: the G5 rerun promise (the program runs again on fresh inputs of the same layout), stated without naming any branch as tricky (LEVER_RULES v3 G5). Naming which axes change is allowed by QC but off by default: mention only what is necessary, no axis list (QL 26 Oct). Keep the G5 ban on "at other scales" phrasing.
28:9. Leave author notes in any agent-visible file (`instruction.md`, `environment/`): no TRAP, trap list, lever, inverse, decoy, grader, hidden test, answer key or author-note wording, including in comments, file names and data fields. precheck.sh greps for them; a hit is a finding.
30:11. Ship any answer for a graded document in `environment/` (LEVER_RULES W11): no answer key, golden or sample output, solved list, expected figure or claimed total, even one that agrees with the contract. Shipped controls reconcile under both readings (W7). Exceptions: one unlabelled L11 witness per lever, and at most one toy worked example per rule on invented values that appear in no shipped or hidden file (W6 v3). Never ship an oracle that contradicts any sentence of the written contract (wafer 32.58 pts; dispatch QC v6 DS-20).
32:## Always
35:3. Any command that may take more than about 4 minutes (Docker builds, harbor runs, playground with Docker, big data generation) runs as `nohup <cmd> > <log> 2>&1 &`. Poll with waits under 4 minutes (`sleep 200; tail -5 <log>`). Never end your turn while your own job runs.
37:5. Keep `_work/<slug>/TODO.md` (ticks), `PLAN.md` and `LOG.md` (IST timestamp from `TZ=Asia/Kolkata date`, command, exit code, result) up to date as you go, so a compaction loses nothing. After a compaction, re-read them and re-check files before acting.
38:6. After any edit to `environment/data/`: regenerate the `_SHIPPED_DATA` embedding in `tests/test_output.py`, recompute `tests/reward.toml` (`0.5/P` per channel at full float precision) and every sha256 in `solution/TRUTH.md`, then re-run the checks your prompt names. After ANY edit under `tests/` or `solution/`, rewrite TRUTH.md sha256 values by script as your last edit (DS-22); precheck.sh recomputes every `<name>: <sha256>` line in TRUTH.md and fails a mismatch.
