41:9. Shell is zsh on macOS: quote words starting with `=`; there is no `timeout` (use `perl -e 'alarm N; exec @ARGV' <cmd>`); build JSON with python, not echo.
44:12. Every new or split test gets the hygiene checks on itself: one property per check (TS-13), fails on an absence (TS-25), honest-untrippable (TS-14/TS-16), not paying twice for one observable (TS-26). There is no count cap.
47:15. Never import, run or py_compile anything under a bundle's `tests/` or `solution/` without `PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1` or `python3 -B`; a shipped `__pycache__` is a structure fail (S5; emberforge QC v8, master 12:29 regen).
48:16. Solver, kill-test and blind-program runs go in Docker only: `docker run --rm --memory 4g --cpus 2 ...` with a wall cap (`perl -e 'alarm N; exec @ARGV'`). Never run a solver on the host (27 Oct 14:35: three host solver processes took about 185 GB and hung the Mac). Kill your own child processes before you report.
